s were kept on the diets <italic>ad libitum</italic> for 12 weeks. Onion diet and quercetin diet contained equal amounts of quercetin (0.023% quercetin aglycone). Values are means &#x000b1; SD (<italic>n</italic> = 6). Values with different superscripts are significantly different (<italic>p</italic>&#x0003c;0.05).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T5" position="float"><label>Table&#x000a0;5</label><caption><p>TBARS and CEOOH levels in plasma and liver of rats after the feeding period.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Group<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn5">1</xref></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">NC</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">DC</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">DO</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">DQ</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan="5" align="left" rowspan="1">Plasma</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;TBARS (&#x000b5;M)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6.4 &#x000b1; 1.1<sup>a</sup></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">10.0 &#x000b1; 1.9<sup>b</sup></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">8.1 &#x000b1; 1.5<sup>ab</sup></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">8.4 &#x000b1; 1.6<sup>ab</sup></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;CEOOH (nM)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.7 &#x000b1; 0.5<sup>a</sup></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7.4 &#x000b1; 1.5<sup>b</sup></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6.2 &#x000b1; 1.2<sup>b</sup></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6.5 &#x000b1; 1.3<sup>b</sup></td></tr><tr><td colspan="5" align="left" rowspan="1">Liver</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;TBARS (nmol/g of liver)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">128 &#x000b1; 11</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">136 &#x000b1; 16</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">130 &#x000b1; 12</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">132 &#x000b1; 10</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tblfn5"><label>1</label><p>NC, normal rats fed basal diet; DC, diabetic rats fed basal diet; DO, diabetic rats fed onion diet; DQ, diabetic rats fed quercetin diet. Rats were kept on the diets <italic>ad libitum</italic> for 12 weeks. Onion diet and quercetin diet contained equal amounts of quercetin (0.023% quercetin aglycone). Values are means &#x000b1; SD (<italic>n</italic> = 6). Values with different superscripts are significantly different (<italic>p</italic>&#x0003c;0.05).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>